IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: LETTERS THREATENING TO MURDER (the
-- heading, now carrying one section: section 16, "Threats to kill").
--
-- Section 16 is the one offence in the text whose elements are stated in full and whose
-- penalty is stated in full (no ". . ." in the penalty clause).

§ `Letters threatening to murder`

§§ `Section 16: threats to kill`

-- src:20 | 16 Threats to kill.
-- src:21 | A person who without lawful excuse makes to another a threat, intending that that other would fear it would be carried out, to kill that other or a third person shall be guilty of an offence and liable on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 16 (src:20-21)
-- "threat": the person told another person that somebody would be killed.
-- "without lawful excuse": no lawful excuse (the Act does not say what one is, so
--   whether the person had one is a fact they state).
-- "intending that that other would fear it would be carried out": the intention is
--   about the other person's FEAR.  Intending to carry the threat out is a different
--   fact, carried in `meant to carry the threat out`, and the text does not make it an
--   element.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 16` HAS
    `made a threat to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a lawful excuse for making it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended that the other person would fear it would be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the threat was to kill the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the threat was to kill a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meant to carry the threat out` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 16 (src:21)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 16`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16: threats to kill` c MEANS
        c's `made a threat to another person`
    AND NOT (c's `had a lawful excuse for making it`)
    AND c's `intended that the other person would fear it would be carried out`
    AND (   c's `the threat was to kill the other person`
         OR c's `the threat was to kill a third person`)

-- "guilty of an offence": the only classification the section gives.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 16 (src:21)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 16: what the text calls the offence` MEANS `an offence, with no further classification`

-- "liable on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten
-- years": 10 years = 120 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 16 (src:21)
GIVETH A `Mode of trial`
`s 16: how the text says the offence is tried` MEANS `on indictment`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 16 (src:21)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 16: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 120)
